"{\n  \"entities\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Virtual Reality\",\n      \"type\": \"Technology\",\n      \"description\": \"Virtual reality (VR) technology is a computer-generated environment that allows a user to interact with a simulated world, often through a headset and other sensory devices. It has rapidly evolved in recent years, offering new possibilities and opportunities for various industries, including education.\",\n      \"attributes\": {\n        \"Type\": \"Immersive Technology\",\n        \"Application\": \"Education, Training, Entertainment, etc.\",\n        \"Advantages\": \"Creates immersive and engaging learning experiences, democratizes access to high-quality educational resources, enhances student learning outcomes, promotes creativity and critical thinking, fosters a deeper understanding of complex concepts, caters to different learning styles and preferences, provides alternative learning experiences for students with disabilities or learning difficulties\",\n        \"Challenges\": \"Cost of acquiring and maintaining VR equipment and software, potential health and safety risks, need for educator training, motion sickness, eye strain, disorientation, negative effects on students\\\" well-being and learning outcomes\",\n        \"Development\": \"Rapidly evolving, becoming more affordable and widespread\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"historical landmarks\",\n      \"type\": \"Educational Resource\",\n      \"description\": \"Historical landmarks are significant sites that represent important events, periods, or figures in history. They can be explored through immersive virtual tours, enhancing the educational experience for students.\",\n      \"attributes\": {\n        \"Purpose\": \"Educational and Cultural Significance\",\n        \"Accessibility\": \"Enhanced through Virtual Reality\",\n        \"Type\": \"Physical and Virtual\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"historical events\",\n      \"type\": \"Concept\",\n 