h has been decreasing, making the technology more accessible to a wider range of students.\",\n      \"attributes\": {}\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Virtual Field Trips\",\n      \"type\": \"Educational Activity\",\n      \"description\": \"Virtual field trips are simulated experiences that allow students to explore places and environments without physically traveling.\",\n      \"attributes\": {}\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Simulations\",\n      \"type\": \"Educational Activity\",\n      \"description\": \"Simulations in education are computer-generated models that replicate real-world scenarios for learning and training purposes.\",\n      \"attributes\": {}\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Policymakers\",\n      \"type\": \"Professional Group\",\n      \"description\": \"Policymakers are individuals or groups responsible for making decisions and setting guidelines that affect educational practices and policies.\",\n      \"attributes\": {}\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Risks of VR Technology\",\n      \"type\": \"Concept\",\n      \"description\": \"The potential risks associated with the use of virtual reality technology in educational settings, such as privacy concerns, physical safety, and psychological impacts.\",\n      \"attributes\": {}\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Guidelines and Safeguards\",\n      \"type\": \"Policy\",\n      \"description\": \"Policies and protective measures designed to ensure the safe and ethical use of virtual reality technology in educational settings.\",\n      \"attributes\": {}\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Virtual Experiences\",\n      \"type\": \"Educational Activity\",\n      \"description\": \"Educational activities conducted in virtual environments, such as virtual operating rooms for medical students and immersive virtual tours for history students.\",\n      \"attributes\": {}\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Student Learning in VR\",\n      \"type\": \"Educational Outcome\",\n      \"description\": \"The evaluation of students\\\" learning and performance in virtual reality environments.\",\n      \"attributes\": {}\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Students with Disabilities or Learning Difficulties\",\n      \"type\": \"Student Group\",\n      \"description\": \"A group of students who have disabilities or learning difficulties that may require special accommodations or alternative learning methods.\",\n      \"attributes\": {}\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Socio-Economic Backgrounds\",\n      \"type\": \"Social Factor\",\n      \"description\": \"Differences in socio-economic status among students that can affect their access to educational resources and opportunities.\",\n      \"attributes\": {}\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Virtual Reality Technology\",\n      \"type\": \"Technology\",\n      \"description\": \"Virtual Reality (VR) technology creates a simulated environment that can be experienced through a device, allowing users to interact with this virtual world.\",\n      \"attributes\": {}\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Professional Development Programs\",\n      \"type\": \"Educational Resource\",\n      \"description\": \"Professional development programs are designed to enhance the skills and knowledge of teachers, helping them to better utilize new educational tools and methods.\",\n      \"attributes\": {}\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Students\",\n      \"type\": \"Educational Recipient\",\n      \"description\": \"Students are individuals who attend educational institutions to learn and gain knowledge. They benefit from the innovative teaching methods and technologies introduced by their teachers.\",\n      \"attributes\": {}\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"creativity and critical thinking\",\n      \"type\": \"Cognitive Skills\",\n      \"description\": \"Creativity and critical thinking are higher-order cognitive skills that involve generating and applying new ideas and analyzing information to form reasoned judgments.\